      "side": 1,
      "message": "The byte-overlap counting still looks right to me, and native VMAs get the same `first`, `last` and byte count as before.\n\nI think the move from PS13 got lost in a later patchset, though. The reply there says the 4KB counting went into `vma_shmem_swap_usage()` in `include/linux/p3s/shmem.h`, but PS27 has no such header. Instead, `shmem_partial_swap_usage()` now takes the VMA, the 4KB branches run inside the native loop, and `shmem_swap_usage()` has `vma_is_p3s_4k()` in its fast-path condition again. That adds 39 lines to `mm/shmem.c` and changes the upstream prototype in `\u003clinux/shmem_fs.h\u003e`.\n\nWould you mind moving the 4KB path back into a static inline in a new `include/linux/p3s/shmem.h`, with a stub returning 0 in the `#else` branch of its `#ifdef CONFIG_ARM64_PER_PROCESS_PAGE_SIZE` block? Something like:\n\n```\nstatic inline unsigned long vma_shmem_swap_usage(struct vm_area_struct *vma,\n\t\t\t\t\t\t unsigned long start,\n\t\t\t\t\t\t unsigned long end)\n```\n\n`shmem_partial_swap_usage()`, its prototype and its callers could then stay as upstream has them, and `shmem_swap_usage()` would only need an early return after the `!swapped` check:\n\n```\n\tif (vma_is_p3s_4k(vma))\n\t\treturn vma_shmem_swap_usage(vma, vma-\u003evm_start, vma-\u003evm_end);\n```\n\nThat also takes care of the extern and alignment CHECKs from checkpatch, since those upstream lines would no longer change.",
